@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP systems. Correct information/store ownership and prevent future execution or shared core/Git stores.
title MVP DFD — core and separate ProjectForge information owners
skinparam backgroundColor #0D1525
skinparam defaultFontColor #EDF4FF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam wrapWidth 190
actor "User / browser" as U
actor "Native Git client" as CL
rectangle "Resumefolio core" {
 rectangle "Core dashboard / permitted adapter" as C
 rectangle "F09 private media / policy / recovery" as F
 database "Core records and private same-server bytes" as D
 F --> D : owned file / reference / operation data
}
rectangle "ProjectForge — separate system" {
 rectangle "F06 issues / simple Kanban" as W
 rectangle "F07 repository access / file-history" as G
 database "ProjectForge state / native repositories\nPhysical database/placement undecided" as GD
 W --> GD : owned board / issue state
 G --> GD : native objects / refs
}
U --> C
C <--> W : authenticated user-scoped API
C <--> G : authenticated user-scoped API
CL --> G : real native transfer\nclient-created commits
rectangle "AFTER MVP: F05 private communications / advanced F06 and F07 / F08 execution" as FUT #4A302B
legend bottom
 Arrows carry information; they imply no common database, cross-system SQL transaction or permission inheritance.
endlegend
@enduml
